WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.902
Here is the short version.

00:00:01.902 --> 00:00:04.390
AI coding tools made output cheap.

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:10.902
Bubbles is for the part that stayed expensive: knowing whether the work is actually done.

00:00:10.902 --> 00:00:22.974
It is a framework around VS Code Copilot Chat that adds specialist agents, workflow modes, repo-local instructions, artifacts, validation gates, and evidence trails.

00:00:22.974 --> 00:00:25.461
For developers, it reduces rework.

00:00:25.461 --> 00:00:28.827
For managers, it makes status less mysterious.

00:00:28.827 --> 00:00:36.363
For leadership, it turns AI coding from a pile of clever conversations into a governed delivery system.

00:00:36.363 --> 00:00:38.163
Still practical.

00:00:38.163 --> 00:00:40.460
Still funny enough to survive a standup.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:43.692
The core problem is not that AI is too slow.

00:00:43.692 --> 00:00:51.112
It is that AI is fast enough to create a convincing mess before anybody has checked the blast radius.

00:00:51.112 --> 00:00:52.948
The output looks serious.

00:00:52.948 --> 00:00:55.225
The summary sounds responsible.

00:00:55.225 --> 00:00:57.943
But did the agent run the real tests?

00:00:57.943 --> 00:00:59.743
Did it update the spec?

00:00:59.743 --> 00:01:02.388
Did it call an endpoint that exists?

00:01:02.388 --> 00:01:06.428
Did it break a workflow nobody mentioned in the prompt?

00:01:06.428 --> 00:01:11.864
Bubbles exists for that gap between code generation and verified delivery.

00:01:11.864 --> 00:01:19.100
It asks the annoying question every serious project eventually asks: cool story, where is the proof?

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:21.907
For developers, the pain is practical.

00:01:21.907 --> 00:01:24.345
The agent changes a lot of files.

00:01:24.345 --> 00:01:34.688
You spend the next hour figuring out what is real, what is accidental, and why the test suite suddenly behaves like a witness with a lawyer.

00:01:34.688 --> 00:01:37.052
Bubbles gives that work a trail.

00:01:37.052 --> 00:01:39.194
Analyst captures the outcome.

00:01:39.194 --> 00:01:41.263
Design names the safe shape.

00:01:41.263 --> 00:01:43.063
Plan slices the work.

00:01:43.063 --> 00:01:44.863
Implement changes code.

00:01:44.863 --> 00:01:46.663
Test verifies behavior.

00:01:46.663 --> 00:01:48.657
Docs updates durable truth.

00:01:48.657 --> 00:01:52.056
Validate checks whether the claim can advance.

00:01:52.056 --> 00:01:54.863
That does not make development slower.

00:01:54.863 --> 00:01:56.784
It reduces the rework tax.

00:01:56.784 --> 00:02:00.840
The useful kind of strict is the kind that saves your Friday.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:03.362
How does it solve developer problems?

00:02:03.362 --> 00:02:05.883
By making the proof part of the loop.

00:02:05.883 --> 00:02:11.677
If the UI calls a route from a dream sequence, vertical slice checks should catch it.

00:02:11.677 --> 00:02:18.151
If a regression test only passes because it avoids the old bug, quality guards should complain.

00:02:18.151 --> 00:02:24.626
If the first implementation works but leaves duplicated logic everywhere, simplify gets a turn.

00:02:24.626 --> 00:02:28.238
The normal entry point is slash bubbles dot workflow.

00:02:28.238 --> 00:02:30.038
Describe the outcome.

00:02:30.038 --> 00:02:34.537
Bubbles routes the phases and keeps evidence attached to the work.

00:02:34.537 --> 00:02:36.718
You still write and review code.

00:02:36.718 --> 00:02:41.352
You just stop accepting a confident paragraph as the build artifact.

00:02:41.352 --> 00:02:42.960
A beautiful lifestyle change.

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:46.359
For managers, the problem is not typing speed.

00:02:46.359 --> 00:02:48.206
It is inspectable status.

00:02:48.206 --> 00:02:53.674
Is this feature done, or did the agent just reach the end of the chat box?

00:02:53.674 --> 00:02:55.474
Which scenarios passed?

00:02:55.474 --> 00:02:57.274
Which risks remain?

00:02:57.274 --> 00:02:59.074
Which docs changed?

00:02:59.074 --> 00:03:01.143
Which scopes are still open?

00:03:01.143 --> 00:03:04.837
Bubbles turns that into artifacts you can inspect.

00:03:04.837 --> 00:03:06.637
Scopes explain the work.

00:03:06.637 --> 00:03:10.406
Definition of done items say what completion means.

00:03:10.406 --> 00:03:13.435
Reports show command output and evidence.

00:03:13.435 --> 00:03:15.235
State records progress.

00:03:15.235 --> 00:03:20.334
Validation gates can block a status transition when proof is missing.

00:03:20.334 --> 00:03:27.058
That makes status less like weather forecasting and more like reading the instrument panel.

00:03:27.058 --> 00:03:29.880
Still imperfect, but at least the knobs are labeled.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:40.848
Planning drift is what happens when one assistant tries to be product analyst, architect, implementer, tester, auditor, and release manager all at once.

00:03:40.848 --> 00:03:42.648
It can sound impressive.

00:03:42.648 --> 00:03:47.554
It can also turn a simple bug into a scenic tour of unrelated files.

00:03:47.554 --> 00:03:49.574
Bubbles separates ownership.

00:03:49.574 --> 00:03:51.595
Analyst owns business truth.

00:03:51.595 --> 00:03:53.399
Design owns architecture.

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:55.419
Plan owns executable scopes.

00:03:55.419 --> 00:03:57.219
Implement implements.

00:03:57.219 --> 00:03:59.019
Test tests.

00:03:59.019 --> 00:04:00.819
Validate certifies.

00:04:00.819 --> 00:04:02.619
Audit reviews.

00:04:02.619 --> 00:04:11.061
Managers get a clearer operating model: who owns the artifact, what gate blocked the work, and what must happen next.

00:04:11.061 --> 00:04:16.420
That is much better than asking, why did the chatbot rewrite our onboarding copy while fixing a database lock?

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:19.186
For leadership, the question is bigger.

00:04:19.186 --> 00:04:25.498
How do we use AI coding tools without turning every repository into a private experiment?

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:33.229
How do we get speed without losing compliance, quality signals, release discipline, and institutional memory?

00:04:33.229 --> 00:04:35.428
Bubbles gives control surfaces.

00:04:35.428 --> 00:04:37.343
The rules live in the repo.

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:40.676
The workflow modes encode how work should move.

00:04:40.676 --> 00:04:42.476
Gates make risk visible.

00:04:42.476 --> 00:04:49.427
Security, audit, release, retro, and hotspot analysis can become part of the same operating model.

00:04:49.427 --> 00:04:52.335
It does not replace engineering judgment.

00:04:52.335 --> 00:05:00.890
It gives engineering judgment a repeatable rail system so AI help does not become unmanaged enthusiasm with commit access.

00:05:00.890 --> 00:05:04.303
The trick is governance without freezing delivery.

00:05:04.303 --> 00:05:12.835
A twenty-page policy PDF does not help if the agent never reads it and developers only remember it during an incident review.

00:05:12.835 --> 00:05:20.752
Bubbles keeps policy close to the work: instructions, skills, templates, workflows, and gates inside the repository.

00:05:20.752 --> 00:05:26.076
That means the agent can be guided by the same standards the team cares about.

00:05:26.076 --> 00:05:38.430
Leadership gets a path to scale AI-assisted delivery with fewer blind spots: not by slowing everyone down, but by making proof, ownership, and validation part of the default motion.

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:40.517
Here is a concrete example.

00:05:40.517 --> 00:05:44.844
Checkout fails when availability changes during payment.

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:55.663
Without structure, the agent patches a handler, adds a happy-path test, says done, and the race condition returns next week with sunglasses.

00:05:55.663 --> 00:06:00.609
With Bubbles, the workflow starts with the user-visible outcome.

00:06:00.609 --> 00:06:03.546
Design names the transaction boundary.

00:06:03.546 --> 00:06:06.714
Plan defines scenarios and done criteria.

00:06:06.714 --> 00:06:09.264
Implement changes the right path.

00:06:09.264 --> 00:06:11.660
Test adds adversarial coverage.

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:13.460
Chaos can poke timing.

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:15.392
Validate checks evidence.

00:06:15.392 --> 00:06:17.401
Audit names residual risk.

00:06:17.401 --> 00:06:19.201
Same AI coding help.

00:06:19.201 --> 00:06:21.519
Very different operating loop.

00:06:21.519 --> 00:06:23.760
One future gives you a patch.

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:27.270
The other gives you a reason to believe the patch.

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:30.340
The starting path is intentionally small.

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:32.140
Do not boil the ocean.

00:06:32.140 --> 00:06:43.371
Pick one painful workflow: a bug that keeps coming back, a feature with drifting requirements, or a release packet that always turns into archaeology.

00:06:43.371 --> 00:06:45.617
Install and bootstrap Bubbles.

00:06:45.617 --> 00:06:47.417
Run doctor.

00:06:47.417 --> 00:06:51.610
Ask slash bubbles dot super if you do not know the move.

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:55.129
Use slash bubbles dot workflow for normal work.

00:06:55.129 --> 00:06:59.621
Use goal, sprint, and releases when the outcome gets bigger.

00:06:59.621 --> 00:07:02.916
Then judge the system by the evidence trail.

00:07:02.916 --> 00:07:04.716
Not by charm.

00:07:04.716 --> 00:07:05.530
Not by vibes.

00:07:05.530 --> 00:07:05.530
By what it can show you.

00:07:05.530 --> 00:07:09.118
The win is not that Bubbles makes agents magical.

00:07:09.118 --> 00:07:10.918
Magic is hard to debug.

00:07:10.918 --> 00:07:19.045
The win is that agents can take bigger swings while the work stays reviewable, recoverable, and safer to trust.

00:07:19.045 --> 00:07:21.461
Developers get less cleanup debt.

00:07:21.461 --> 00:07:24.463
Managers get clearer status and evidence.

00:07:24.463 --> 00:07:29.589
Leadership gets a practical governance layer for AI-assisted delivery.

00:07:29.589 --> 00:07:31.389
Output is cheap now.

00:07:31.389 --> 00:07:33.292
Verified work is valuable.

00:07:33.292 --> 00:07:41.127
Bubbles is the system that tries to turn one into the other, without making everybody wear a committee hat.

00:07:41.127 --> 00:07:42.957
That is the introduction.

00:07:42.957 --> 00:07:44.757
That is the pitch.

00:07:44.757 --> 00:07:46.020
And honestly, that is the job.
